{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-102675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $AB=BA={I}_{2}$\n- $AC=CA={I}_{2}$\n- $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-102675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement III is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-102675" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3522ef3314fed4769b534aa0321a492bb17fa48739bc3084445e43602ed2edec"} {"question" "q-102675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-102675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-102675" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II and III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,D=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- $CD=DC={I}_{2}$\n- $DE=ED={I}_{2}$\n- $D={C}^{-1}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "- First, we check whether $CD=DC={I}_{2}.$ Computing $CD$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $DC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DC & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement I is true. As a result, $D={C}^{-1}$ and statement III is true too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $DE=ED={I}_{2}.$ Computing $DE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}DE & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}∗ & ∗ \\\\ -2 & ∗\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only\"." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3522ef3314fed4769b534aa0321a492bb17fa48739bc3084445e43602ed2edec"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13974727/state.json" "file_sha256" "f452d13e82fee23c4dd18245193f4980340e72913b5d3a7174cd16c6fcdeb802"} {"question" "q-11637" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "va