" {"q-11640" [] "e-4499" [] "q-7913" [] "e-4500" []} "basis" 763 "retractions" [[17592186087925 :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n$B = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}, D = \\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $BC = CB = I_{2}$\n2. $BD = DB = I_{2}$\n3. $D = B^{-1}$"] [17592186088311 :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -6 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 7 & -6\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\n1. $AB = BA = I_{4}$\n2. $AC = CA = I_{4}$\n3. $B = A^{-1}$"] [17592186087441 :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087441 :question/worked-solution "We must check whether\n\n$$\nAB = BA = I_2\n$$\n\nComputing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{2}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}$."] [17592186087442 :question/problem "Using the method of direct verification, determine whether the matrix $B$ is the inverse of $A$, where\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [17592186087442 :question/worked-solution "First, we check whether\n\n$$\nAB = BA = I_3\n$$\n\nComputing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{3}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $BA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBA &= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= I_{3}.✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $B = A^{-1}$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186084562 17592186084563 17592186084564 17592186084565 17592186084566 17592186086797 17592186086798 17592186086799 17592186086800 17592186086801] "immutable_fields" [[17592186084561 :answer-field/correct] [17592186084561 :answer-field/id] [17592186084561 :answer-field/key] [17592186084561 :answer-field/type] [17592186086796 :answer-field/correct] [17592186086796 :answer-field/id] [17592186086796 :answer-field/key] [17592186086796 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
